      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fb9b5d70e960412ee36b56b|full_name}: Currently the only way to manage this issue is to have the auto-resync off and use a custom script, which on some interval of time (like 5 minutes or whatever) sets the video player time to the current time + some minor amount (like 0.1f). Because the auto-resync doesn't have a configurable interval option yet (like I suggested here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1112-videoplayer-audio-video-resync-is-causing-significant-hitching-during-playb ) it will either be users eventually desyncing or sub par playback due to the regularly occurring hitches caused by the forced resync, at least without a custom solution which is what I did for my VP.\nI would like to submit for reconsideration to the devs, adding an configurable interval value for the automatic resync and then making sure it is exposed to udon. As that would alleviate the binary issue of desync vs video hitching by giving creators control of how often they want to forcefully resync the media.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
